<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/socratic-method> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A method of inquiry by disciplined question and answer, modelled on Socrates in Plato's dialogues, in which a person's stated belief is examined against their other commitments until inconsistencies, hidden assumptions or gaps in their reasons come to light; used today in teaching, law schools and cognitive therapy." .
