<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/sophistical-refutations> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aristotle's short treatise (4th century BCE), the last work of the Organon and a closing section of the Topics, on arguments that only appear to refute a thesis; its list of thirteen fallacies, six dependent on language and seven not, is the first systematic theory of fallacies and the root of the traditional fallacy lists still taught today." .
