<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/william-whewell> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "English philosopher, historian of science and Master of Trinity College, Cambridge (1794-1866), who built a theory of scientific induction from the history of the sciences, proposed prediction of new phenomena and the \"consilience of inductions\" as tests of a theory, debated John Stuart Mill on induction, and coined the word \"scientist\"." .
